<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximiliano Hernández Martínez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1882">1882</a>–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximiliano Hernández Martínez was a Salvadoran general and dictator, president of El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> from 1931 to 1944. In 1932 his regime crushed a peasant uprising in western El Salvador in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-matanza">La Matanza</a>, killing thousands, many of them indigenous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pipil">Pipil</a>. He ruled through the army until a general strike forced him out in 1944, and he was killed in exile in Honduras.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximiliano-hernandez-martinez.jpg" alt="Maximiliano Hernández Martínez" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Maximiliano_Hern%C3%A1ndez_Mart%C3%ADnez,_President_of_El_Salvador.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
